Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(import):=20keyed,=20atomic=20CAS=20reconci?=
 =?UTF-8?q?le=20=E2=80=94=20NSDL/CDSL/CAMS=20coexist,=20ids=20survive=20re?=
 =?UTF-8?q?-import,=20diff=20preview?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1 — data model & integrity
- migrations/0029_cas_natural_key.sql: depository / account_id / isin /
  holding_status columns, unique natural key on CAS rows, LEGACY backfill,
  apply_cas_snapshot() RPC (single transaction: upsert on key, exit detection
  scoped to the accounts in the statement, soft-exit rows with dependents,
  hard-delete the rest, never let an older statement regress a newer one,
  retire pre-upgrade LEGACY rows). Tested against Postgres 16.
- cas_casparser_service.py: ISIN dedup is now per demat account (same stock
  in two DPs was being dropped), real account_id (dpid/clientid | folio |
  MF-FOLIOS), depository from casparser file_type (was cas_type =
  SUMMARY/DETAILED), same-folio duplicate schemes merged, parse_warnings
  surfaced, JSON password-list mode.
- services/casImport.service.js + lib/casDiff.js: shared preview/apply used by
  both the upload route and the Gmail cron (which had its own flush-and-fill).
- holdings.service.js: CAS path delegates to the RPC; CSV/manual dedup key is
  now per member (two members holding the same ticker collided); NULL-safe
  source filter; parallel updates; transaction note no longer says "CSV" for
  every source; list() and snapshot exclude soft-exited rows.

Phase 2 — UX & optimisations
- POST /api/holdings/import/preview: new / changed(+delta) / unchanged /
  reentered / older, exits, cross-source overlaps (MF double-count guard with
  per-row skip), legacy rows, unmatched holders, already-imported detection.
- CASImportModal: diff summary, status column, exit list, overlap toggles,
  legacy-replace checkbox, duplicate-statement banner; import button waits for
  the preview; failure message states nothing was written.
- Single-process password unlock: one Python spawn tries "", typed, and all
  stored PANs (was one spawn + full parse per candidate).
- statement_hash (sha256 of PDF) stored in import_logs; Gmail cron skips a
  PDF it has already applied.

Tests: tests/casDiff.test.js, tests/casImport.service.test.js (64 total pass).

